<p><strong>The Brown Quantum Initiative (BQI) is the hub for Quantum Science and Engineering research at Brown.</strong> 
We celebrate Brown’s cross-disciplinary values by bringing together Faculty, Postdocs, and Graduate Students across several Departments to discuss novel Quantum research and collaborate on challenging academic projects.</p>

<p>In the 2024–25 academic year, <strong>we are responsible for the weekly Brown Interdisciplinary Quantum Seminar Series</strong>. 
Each seminar features a Brown or external speakers working on at least one of the many fields that intersect in Quantum Science and Engineering. 
<strong>To propose a talk or learn more about the seminar series please visit the</strong> <a href="/seminar.html">Brown Interdisciplinary Quantum Seminar Series site</a>.
Some previous talks can be found in <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@BrownQuantumInitiative">our YouTube channel</a>.</p>

<p><strong>To get emails about new talks and other news about Quantum Science and Engineering at Brown, you can request to join our mailing list/Google Group by following</strong> <a href="https://groups.google.com/u/1/a/brown.edu/g/brown-quantum-initiative">this link</a>.</p>

<p><strong>Time and Location</strong><br />All talks are held from <strong>noon to 1PM on Wednesdays</strong> in <strong>CIT 241</strong> unless otherwise stated.</p>

